{
  // `npm run typecheck` uses tsconfig.json, whose `include` is src/** only —
  // correct for the build, since tests must never reach dist. The effect was that
  // nothing typechecked the tests: vitest transpiles without checking, and
  // Stryker's typescript checker points at the build config too. A type error in
  // any test file passed every CI leg unnoticed.
  //
  // This config adds them without emitting, so `typecheck` covers both. It also
  // picks up tests/surface.test-d.ts, whose `@ts-expect-error` lines are the only
  // guard that the public surface has not widened — vitest never runs that file.
  //
  // Two things are deliberately NOT listed, because listing a path that
  // contributes no files claims a coverage that does not exist:
  //
  //   scripts/  — holds only e2e.mjs and verify-consumer.sh, and `allowJs` is off,
  //               so it contributed zero files. e2e.mjs is a hand-run script
  //               against production; checking it means turning on allowJs
  //               project-wide.
  //   *.json    — stryker.config.json was listed here and also contributed
  //               nothing: `resolveJsonModule` is off, and a config file is not
  //               reachable from any import anyway.
  //
  // Verify with: npx tsc -p tsconfig.test.json --listFiles
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["node", "vitest/globals"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "tests/**/*", "vitest.config.ts"]
}
